{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7bfbef"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edf6a3fc", "timestamp": "2027-02-22T20:07:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Insufficient Model Access Logging' has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/EdgeForce/pull/44.", "utterranceID": "20270222-0-7435a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270222-0-7435a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7bfbef"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edf6a3fc", "timestamp": "2027-02-22T20:08:00", "text": "The root cause was that our logging mechanism wasn't capturing detailed access events or anomalies, which made it difficult to audit and respond to any unauthorized access or tampering.", "utterranceID": "20270222-1-ebb74"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270222-1-ebb74"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7bfbef"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edf6a3fc", "timestamp": "2027-02-22T20:09:00", "text": "To fix this, I implemented a more comprehensive logging system that now records detailed access events, including timestamps, user IDs, and any anomalies detected during access. This should significantly improve our ability to monitor and audit access to the AI models.", "utterranceID": "20270222-2-2ef52"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270222-2-2ef52"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7bfbef"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2347b567", "timestamp": "2027-02-22T20:12:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_edf6a3fc! This will definitely help us in maintaining better security and compliance. Thanks for the quick turnaround.", "utterranceID": "20270222-3-17616"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270222-3-17616"}

